    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests {@link InternationalFixedDate#range(TemporalField)}. <p> In the International Fixed calendar the Leap Day (month 6, day 29 of a leap year) and the Year Day (month 13, day 29) stand outside the normal week structure. As a result, every \"week-based\" field reports the empty range {@code [0, 0]} for those two days, while ordinary days report their usual ranges. These tests pin down that behaviour field by field."
   },
   {
    "id": "i2",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     29,
     31
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Asserts that the given date reports the expected range for the given field."
   },
